TEXT 48 -560 Left 3 ;#104 Adjustable sawtooth generator
TEXT 48 -496 Left 2 ;Source: Alan Wolke (W2AEW), https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ibnz5UjQ4u0
TEXT 48 -448 Left 2 ;Complementary current sources and a diode bridge alternately charge and discharge Ctiming; a hysteretic comparator reverses the slopes.
TEXT 1920 -368 Left 2 !.param RRISE=500 RFALL=500
TEXT 1920 -320 Left 2 !.ic V(RAMP)=0
TEXT 1920 -272 Left 2 !.tran 0 5m 0 100n
TEXT 1920 -200 Left 2 !.meas tran RAMP_MAX MAX V(RAMP) FROM 2m TO 5m
TEXT 1920 -160 Left 2 !.meas tran RAMP_MIN MIN V(RAMP) FROM 2m TO 5m
TEXT 1920 -120 Left 2 !.meas tran TC1 WHEN V(CTRL)=4.5 RISE=3
TEXT 1920 -80 Left 2 !.meas tran TC2 WHEN V(CTRL)=4.5 RISE=4
TEXT 1920 -40 Left 2 !.meas tran PERIOD PARAM TC2-TC1
TEXT 1920 0 Left 2 !.meas tran FREQ PARAM 1/(TC2-TC1)
TEXT 1920 40 Left 2 !.meas tran TR_LO WHEN V(RAMP)=3.5 RISE=3
TEXT 1920 80 Left 2 !.meas tran TR_HI WHEN V(RAMP)=5.5 RISE=3
TEXT 1920 120 Left 2 !.meas tran RISE_SLOPE PARAM 2/(TR_HI-TR_LO)
TEXT 1920 160 Left 2 !.meas tran TF_HI WHEN V(RAMP)=5.5 FALL=3
TEXT 1920 200 Left 2 !.meas tran TF_LO WHEN V(RAMP)=3.5 FALL=3
TEXT 1920 240 Left 2 !.meas tran FALL_SLOPE PARAM 2/(TF_LO-TF_HI)
TEXT 1920 320 Left 2 ;All of Alan's values are used as drawn: the two 1k\nadjustments with their 180 ohm series resistors, the\n1k reference resistor, three 3.9k resistors around the\ncomparator, 0.1 uF of timing capacitance, and 1N4148\nbridge diodes.
TEXT 1920 512 Left 2 ;Alan writes "all diodes: 1N4198" on his sheet, which is\nnot a catalog part; 1N4148 is the evident reading and\nis what the simulation uses.
TEXT 1920 640 Left 2 ;He states that he used a rail-to-rail output op amp and\nthat it is adequate at this speed, but names no part. The\n9 V rail, the 2N3904 and 2N3906, the op amp macromodels\nand the 100k load are simulation choices.
TEXT 1920 832 Left 2 ;RRISE and RFALL stand for the two 1k adjustments, at\ntheir mid positions here. Change either between 0 and\n1000 to set that slope on its own, which is the whole\npoint of the circuit.
